{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794763093","published":"2026-11-15T17:18:36Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:35.839660535Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-116304","CVE-2026-116306","CVE-2026-116307","CVE-2026-116309","CVE-2026-116314","CVE-2026-116315","CVE-2026-116316","CVE-2026-116317","CVE-2026-116319","CVE-2026-116320","CVE-2026-116323","CVE-2026-116326","CVE-2026-116330","CVE-2026-116331","CVE-2026-116332","CVE-2026-116335","CVE-2026-116336","CVE-2026-120139","CVE-2026-120141","CVE-2026-120143","CVE-2026-120145","CVE-2026-120147","CVE-2026-120150","CVE-2026-120151","CVE-2026-120153","CVE-2026-14661","CVE-2026-18447","CVE-2026-6460","CVE-2026-6467"],"summary":"postgresql: Fix of 29 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-116309: plperl: fix type confusion and a NULL pointer dereference\n  in get_perl_array_ref() for forged array objects\n- CVE-2026-116326: plperl: support tied Perl objects in plperl, hstore_plperl\n  and jsonb_plperl, cope with errors thrown from tied structures and harden\n  against tied-scalar mischief\n- CVE-2026-116320: plperl: hold a reference on a Perl array or hash while\n  scanning it\n- CVE-2026-116319: plperl: don't save and re-use the temporary context in\n  return_next()\n- CVE-2026-116307: plperl: refuse to free a prepared query that is being\n  executed\n- CVE-2026-116304: fix a possible use-after-free in\n  find_or_make_matching_shared_tupledesc()\n- CVE-2026-116306: handle composite type changes in\n  ExecEvalFieldStoreDeForm/ExecEvalFieldStoreForm\n- CVE-2026-116314: pg_restore: fix out-of-bounds accesses and path traversal\n- CVE-2026-116315: fix a potential buffer overrun in tsvector_delete()\n- CVE-2026-116317: fix a potential buffer overrun in ts_rank_cd()\n- CVE-2026-116323: pltcl: avoid use-after-free hazards in re-entrant use\n- CVE-2026-116330: make \\restrict keys protective in pg_dump --format=tar\n  restore.sql\n- CVE-2026-116331: don't use MinMaxAggPath if the aggregate's input and output\n  types don't match\n- CVE-2026-116332: fix use-after-free issues due to dropping portals that are\n  being set up\n- CVE-2026-116335: check that commutator/negator operators return the same\n  data type\n- CVE-2026-120141: fix type confusion with materialized set-returning\n  functions\n- CVE-2026-120143: close portals at the end of trigger functions with\n  transition tables\n- CVE-2026-120147: dblink: refuse to use a connection that a dblink call is\n  already using\n- CVE-2026-120150: avoid using a dangling pointer in expanded-record domain\n  checks\n- CVE-2026-120151: plpgsql: recheck a record field's type after casting the\n  value\n- CVE-2026-120153: reject more unsafe names in extension script substitutions\n- CVE-2026-6467: block the ALTER SCHEMA RENAME attack on CREATE EXTENSION and\n  friends by locking, and reject a temporary or '$user' extension schema\n- CVE-2026-14661: validate all connection options for dblink, postgres_fdw and\n  logical replication before connecting, blocking unsafe and unknown options\n  such as libpq 18's sslkeylogfile and oauth_*\n- CVE-2026-18447: reject pseudo-type output parameters in SQL functions\n- CVE-2026-116316: prevent creating types in pg_temp from security-restricted\n  code\n- CVE-2026-116336: fix a crash in REINDEX CONCURRENTLY due to DDL run in index\n  functions\n- CVE-2026-120139: protect against miscalculation of tuple sizes via int32\n  overflow and harden some allocations against integer wraparound\n- CVE-2026-120145: reject system catalogs as logical replication targets\n- CVE-2026-6460: forbid ALTERing a column or composite type used by stored\n  expressions, defaults, constraints or indexes; fix related locking races\n  (partial mitigation)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"postgresql","ecosystem":"TuxCare:RHEL:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/postgresql?distro=rhel-8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"13.23-3.module_el8+2811+8e5fd2e3.tuxcare.els8"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tu